Review written to `docs/reviews/py-binding/py-binding-04-py-control-binding.md`.

Summary of findings:

- **1 critical**: No numeric-range validation on any ControlSignal constructor — negative absolute power limits, out-of-range fractions, negative SOC targets all pass silently instead of raising `PyValueError`.

- **2 high**: (1) `apply_control()` hardcodes `Schedule` priority with no way to set tier from Python, and (2) `PySignal` enum for actor dispatch is missing 11 of 25 `ControlSignal` variants.

- **3 medium**: Missing `component` param on `PyDispatchRequest.duty_cycle()`, strict f64 equality in OCHRE self-consumption compat, and no price-signal variant in ControlSignal (routed through separate `set_price_signal` API).

- **3 low**: Misleading test name, stale test comments, and no "auto"/"schedule" mode support.
